{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CfgSaUjTht7VvFzBHP5G8","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"I wrote the candidate, and the self-check prints `OK`. It refines the incumbent `person_pattern_sensitivity_rule_built`, under the name `correlated_tally_switch_attention`.\n\n**The change:** In the incumbent, how sensitive a person is to the tally span and how much they weight switching are two separate, independent traits. Here they share one underlying trait, attention to the sequence's statistics, and the model estimates how strongly the two go together. So someone who tracks the tally closely also tracks switching closely, and someone who barely uses one barely uses the other. Everything else is the incumbent unchanged: the span and switching cues, chunk variety and the rule-built penalty scaled by personal pattern sensitivity, and the left/right lean.\n\n**Why:** It targets the critique that people differ more than the model allows in how often they agree with the majority, even on pairs where pattern structure can't matter. Linking the two cue weights means some people follow both cues consistently and others neither, which widens that spread. This critique result is weak, though: raw p = 0.04, and it does not survive the FDR correction (q = 0.32).\n\n**Self-check:** The quick test fit (100 draws, one chain, 224 s) gave a finite ELPD-LOO of −3282.0, close to the incumbent's −3285.7. That number isn't comparable to a full fit. Three things are still open:\n- **Unreliable LOO on the test fit:** 12.7% of trials had a high Pareto k, well above the 1% tolerance. That may just be the short single-chain fit, but it may also mean the ELPD won't be trusted at admission.\n- **Novelty:** if the fitted link between the two traits comes out near zero, predictions will closely match the incumbent's and the novelty gate could reject the model.\n- **Convergence and speed:** the check doesn't test these. The full fit must converge (R-hat ≤ 1.05, ESS ≥ 100) within the 30-minute limit per sampling run.\n\nFiles are in `iter_2/candidate_4/`:\n- `hypothesis.md`\n- `model_name.txt`\n- `candidate.py`"}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2461,"cache_read_input_tokens":84002,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":2461,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":700,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"e0558b4a-9fb8-4c4d-b6ef-4f812405edef","uuid":"ee46e3f0-4678-45f9-8d5e-3d18f3b78c7c","timestamp":"2026-10-04T02:54:08.511Z","request_id":"req_011CfgSaUKQuanay5FezpPaW"}
